# SEAM — governing rules

Governing docs (re-read the relevant section before implementing):
`docs/SEAM_research_blueprint.md`, `docs/PHASE_MINUS1_IMPLEMENTATION_SPEC.md`,
`docs/hybrid_execution_dse_positioning.md`, `AMENDMENTS.md`, `AUDIT_LOG.md`.

## Platform A (aipc-c1) — fixed facts

- Dell XPS 16 DA16260 · Intel Core Ultra 5 325 (**Panther Lake**, not Lunar Lake)
- 4 P + 4 LP-E · **8 logical CPUs, no SMT** · Xe3 iGPU · NPU 5 · 16 GB LPDDR5X unified · no dGPU
- Windows build 26200 · never size worker pools by heuristic / `cpu_count()`

## Number prohibitions

- Never report **50 TOPS** as achieved NPU throughput (peak INT8 only)
- Never state **~120 GB/s** bandwidth until M2.4 measures it (unverified)
- **180 TOPS** is Platform B aggregate only — never as Platform A or NPU-alone
- **No number without a `run_id`** / manifest. Figures read only from `derived/`

## Integrity

- `raw/` is **write-once**. Never modify a sealed run. Never edit `analysis/` except documented AF-001
- No comparison before A/A + noise floor (`derived/noise_floor.json`)
- Analysis consumes `blinded_label`, never `condition_label`
- Discard policy: log in `AUDIT_LOG.md`; no silent discards
- **No silent retries, exception swallowing, or execution-target fallbacks** (log as events)
- **No per-model prompt tailoring** — invalidates H1
- Configs YAML, hashed into manifests; no magic numbers in code

## Tooling

- Python **3.11+**, full type hints, **ruff + mypy** clean, **pytest** for non-hardware logic
- This host has **no sandbox backend**. Every Shell call needing workspace access MUST use
  `required_permissions: ["all"]`. Verify side effects by reading files back

## Milestone gates

- **M2 blocked until M1 accepted.** No telemetry / LHM / energy code until then
- `topology.verified: false` must **not** be flipped without on-silicon AC-power measurement
  (`python -m seam.topology verify --write` under pinned conditions). Do not invent CPU lists
- Work M0→M1→M2→… in order; show evidence before advancing
- Amendments to pre-registered gates require `AMENDMENTS.md` + owner authorization (see AM-004)
